# Fulcrum: always build and install

After any change under `plugins/fulcrum` (or Fulcrum Bridge that the plugin consumes), **do not finish until the plugin is production-built and installed into the Obsidian vault**. The user reloads Obsidian; they should not have to build locally.

## Required last step

Run from the **git monorepo root** (`obsidian-plugins`), never from the vault copy at `.obsidian/plugins/fulcrum` (that folder has no `package.json`).

```bash
cd /path/to/obsidian-plugins
npm run build:fulcrum:install
```

That runs `tsc` + esbuild, merges CSS, and copies `main.js`, `manifest.json`, and `styles.css` into the vault’s `.obsidian/plugins/fulcrum/` using `OBSIDIAN_VAULT_PATH` or gitignored `.vault-path.local.json`. After install, that vault folder also has `BUILD.txt` — if npm is run there, it prints these instructions instead of failing with missing `package.json`.

